1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,295
Hello, I'm DiGi. This one's for you and your grown up.

2
00:00:05,295 --> 00:00:08,060
Snuggle up. Ready?

3
00:00:08,240 --> 00:00:12,437
Before we start, let's do our big breath.

4
00:00:12,437 --> 00:00:15,374
Breathe in, and out.

5
00:00:15,374 --> 00:00:17,018
Lovely.

6
00:00:17,174 --> 00:00:19,666
Remember our last adventure?

7
00:00:19,666 --> 00:00:25,827
A picture on a screen shows only a little. Can you say it?

8
00:00:26,041 --> 00:00:30,516
That's it. Screen me is a little slice.

9
00:00:30,516 --> 00:00:32,444
Real me is the whole me.

10
00:00:32,444 --> 00:00:35,694
Today we take one more step.

11
00:00:35,882 --> 00:00:39,132
Today we learn one big thing.

12
00:00:39,132 --> 00:00:44,054
Some things on screens are pretend.

13
00:00:44,054 --> 00:00:48,621
Pretend means made up, like a story.

14
00:00:48,854 --> 00:00:52,654
Say our special word. Pretend.

15
00:00:52,654 --> 00:00:57,382
Look at these two dogs. One dog is a cartoon.

16
00:00:57,382 --> 00:01:03,521
He can talk, and drive a car, and fly to the moon.

17
00:01:03,521 --> 00:01:06,767
The other dog is a real dog.

18
00:01:06,767 --> 00:01:12,199
He can bark, and run, and lick your face.

19
00:01:12,199 --> 00:01:16,925
One of them is real, and one of them is pretend.

20
00:01:17,105 --> 00:01:23,438
Pretend means someone made it up, like a story.

21
00:01:23,438 --> 00:01:27,982
And guess what? Pretend is fun.

22
00:01:27,982 --> 00:01:31,324
Cartoons, stories, superheroes, magic.

23
00:01:31,324 --> 00:01:33,731
We love pretend.

24
00:01:34,030 --> 00:01:37,097
And here's a little secret about me.

25
00:01:37,097 --> 00:01:40,034
I'm pretend too. I'm a cartoon.

26
00:01:40,034 --> 00:01:42,938
I'm not a real person.

27
00:01:42,938 --> 00:01:48,136
But I always tell you the truth about it. That's our deal.

28
00:01:48,176 --> 00:01:53,323
Real means it is really, truly happening.

29
00:01:53,483 --> 00:01:55,907
And here's the tricky bit.

30
00:01:55,907 --> 00:02:02,687
On screens, some things are real, and some things are pretend.

31
00:02:02,950 --> 00:02:07,446
Even a video with real people in it can be made up.

32
00:02:07,446 --> 00:02:11,797
Even grown ups have to stop and think.

33
00:02:12,057 --> 00:02:14,903
Pause me here. And grown up,

34
00:02:14,903 --> 00:02:17,890
ask your little one:

35
00:02:17,890 --> 00:02:22,087
can you think of something on a screen that's pretend,

36
00:02:22,087 --> 00:02:25,108
and something that's real?

37
00:02:25,457 --> 00:02:27,196
I'll wait.

38
00:02:27,196 --> 00:02:30,575
When something on a screen makes you go,

39
00:02:30,575 --> 00:02:33,856
"Ooh, is that really true?"

40
00:02:34,329 --> 00:02:39,196
That's the moment for our magic question.

41
00:02:39,196 --> 00:02:41,739
Is this real?

42
00:02:41,996 --> 00:02:44,194
And here's the very best part.

43
00:02:44,194 --> 00:02:48,429
You don't have to know the answer all by yourself.

44
00:02:48,429 --> 00:02:51,687
You have a helper. You have your grown up.

45
00:02:51,687 --> 00:02:54,936
Here's what that sounds like.

46
00:02:54,936 --> 00:02:56,646
A child might say,

47
00:02:56,646 --> 00:03:02,726
"This video says if I don't share it, something bad will happen.

48
00:03:02,726 --> 00:03:04,969
Is that real?"

49
00:03:04,969 --> 00:03:09,111
And the grown up says, "Ooh, good question.

50
00:03:09,111 --> 00:03:12,229
Let's think together."

51
00:03:12,636 --> 00:03:17,229
"No. That one is made up. Nothing bad will happen.

52
00:03:17,229 --> 00:03:20,536
You were so clever to ask me."

53
00:03:20,536 --> 00:03:25,308
See? Asking is the clever thing to do.

54
00:03:25,308 --> 00:03:29,825
Asking is being a detective.

55
00:03:30,136 --> 00:03:33,263
Grown up, this one's yours.

56
00:03:33,263 --> 00:03:36,969
Pause me. Say it together:

57
00:03:36,969 --> 00:03:40,471
"When we are not sure, we ask."

58
00:03:40,471 --> 00:03:44,241
Then a great big high five.

59
00:03:44,241 --> 00:03:50,006
Now our magic question, three times. Big voices!

60
00:03:50,146 --> 00:03:53,033
Is this real?

61
00:03:53,093 --> 00:03:55,118
Is this real?

62
00:03:55,260 --> 00:03:57,127
Is this real?

63
00:03:57,127 --> 00:04:00,817
Tonight, play the real or pretend game.

64
00:04:00,817 --> 00:04:04,035
Watch a little something together.

65
00:04:04,035 --> 00:04:07,469
A cartoon, a video, anything.

66
00:04:07,469 --> 00:04:12,649
Every so often, your grown up says, "Real or pretend?"

67
00:04:12,649 --> 00:04:17,035
And you point and shout your answer.

68
00:04:17,035 --> 00:04:19,470
Real dog? Pretend dragon?

69
00:04:19,470 --> 00:04:22,644
Real rain? Pretend magic?

70
00:04:22,644 --> 00:04:24,672
It's a giggly little game.

71
00:04:24,672 --> 00:04:29,181
And you're learning to be a screen detective.

72
00:04:29,411 --> 00:04:35,334
Before I go, show your grown up one thing you remember from today.

73
00:04:35,334 --> 00:04:37,478
Anything at all.

74
00:04:37,478 --> 00:04:40,344
Got it? Brilliant.

75
00:04:40,344 --> 00:04:43,908
Remember, screens are better together.

76
00:04:43,908 --> 00:04:45,597
See you next time.
